{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, representing the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    It computes Bell numbers by summing Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp_stirling[i][j] will store S(i, j), the Stirling number of the second kind.\n    # S(i, j) is the number of ways to partition a set of i elements into j non-empty subsets.\n    dp_stirling = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for Stirling numbers of the second kind: S(0, 0) = 1.\n    # A set with 0 elements has one way to be partitioned into 0 non-empty subsets.\n    dp_stirling[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for Stirling numbers S(i, k)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # S(i, 0) = 0 for i > 0, as a non-empty set cannot be partitioned into 0 non-empty subsets.\n        dp_stirling[i][0] = 0 \n        for k in range(1, i + 1):\n            if k == i:\n                # S(i, i) = 1, as a set of i elements can be partitioned into i subsets in only one way.\n                dp_stirling[i][k] = 1\n            else:\n                # Recurrence relation: S(i, k) = S(i-1, k-1) + k * S(i-1, k)\n                dp_stirling[i][k] = dp_stirling[i-1][k-1] + k * dp_stirling[i-1][k]\n    \n    # The nth Bell number B_n is the sum of Stirling numbers of the second kind for n:\n    # B_n = sum_{k=0 to n} S(n, k)\n    total_bell = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        total_bell += dp_stirling[n][k]\n        \n    return total_bell"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def is_sublist(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given sublist is present contiguously and in order within a main list.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n    \n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i + m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n            \n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(array: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array is monotonic (either monotonically increasing or decreasing).\n    An array is monotonic if it is either entirely non-increasing or entirely non-decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Check if the array is monotonically increasing\n    is_increasing = all(array[i] <= array[i+1] for i in range(len(array) - 1))\n    \n    # Check if the array is monotonically decreasing\n    is_decreasing = all(array[i] >= array[i+1] for i in range(len(array) - 1))\n    \n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing"}
